1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,760
Some documents are too
big to click together.

2
00:00:02,837 --> 00:00:08,077
The 2026 planner's 365 day
pages came from a script.

3
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:13,123
Today we write one ourselves, a week of
meal pages, and read every line of it.

4
00:00:13,343 --> 00:00:16,486
The purple Generator
button opens two editors.

5
00:00:16,613 --> 00:00:20,333
The left one, Define Templates,
describes how pages look.

6
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:25,109
The right one, Build Hierarchy, lists the
pages and says which template each one

7
00:00:25,109 --> 00:00:25,654
uses.

8
00:00:25,863 --> 00:00:30,043
They're simple editors, with no
line numbers and no autocomplete.

9
00:00:30,155 --> 00:00:32,923
Tab won't indent either, so I use spaces.

10
00:00:32,983 --> 00:00:37,043
The Preset menu loads working
samples; I'll start from empty.

11
00:00:39,682 --> 00:00:42,092
First, the smallest pair that works.

12
00:00:42,144 --> 00:00:46,386
On the left, t is an empty object
that will hold my templates,

13
00:00:46,386 --> 00:00:48,484
and t.day is the first one.

14
00:00:48,687 --> 00:00:52,417
Its id is day: that's the
name pages use to ask for it.

15
00:00:52,518 --> 00:00:55,018
Its name, Day, is what the app shows.

16
00:00:55,152 --> 00:01:00,458
A4_WIDTH and A4_HEIGHT come built into
this script: the page size in points.

17
00:01:00,662 --> 00:01:04,462
Elements, everything on the
page, is an empty list for now.

18
00:01:04,577 --> 00:01:08,087
And the script must hand its
templates back: return t.

19
00:01:08,291 --> 00:01:11,941
On the right, nodes will
hold every page, by its id.

20
00:01:12,021 --> 00:01:14,341
nodes.root is the first page.

21
00:01:15,665 --> 00:01:16,815
Id root.

22
00:01:16,879 --> 00:01:19,909
parentId null, because
nothing sits above it.

23
00:01:19,977 --> 00:01:24,297
Type day: the template's id, which
ties this page to its template.

24
00:01:24,370 --> 00:01:27,110
Title Monday, empty data, no children.

25
00:01:27,314 --> 00:01:30,874
This script returns the pages,
and which one is the root.

26
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:34,157
nodes on its own is
short for nodes: nodes.

27
00:01:34,363 --> 00:01:38,260
Preview runs both scripts in
a sealed sandbox: no network,

28
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:42,003
ten seconds at most, and
your project isn't touched.

29
00:01:42,209 --> 00:01:44,742
One template, used by one page.

30
00:01:44,786 --> 00:01:47,736
The card is the Day
template, drawn for Monday.

31
00:01:47,825 --> 00:01:50,415
It's blank, because elements is empty.

32
00:01:51,025 --> 00:01:53,265
Now the elements, one at a time.

33
00:01:53,338 --> 00:01:55,938
Inside the brackets, a text element.

34
00:01:55,979 --> 00:02:01,979
X 40, y 40 is its top left corner: 40
points from the left edge and from the top.

35
00:02:02,183 --> 00:02:07,297
W 400 and h 50 are the size
of its box, also in points.

36
00:02:07,404 --> 00:02:12,664
The text is {{title}}: each
page fills in its own title.

37
00:02:12,871 --> 00:02:15,161
Font size 32, and bold.

38
00:02:15,196 --> 00:02:19,016
There's no id: the generator
gives each element one.

39
00:02:19,053 --> 00:02:23,944
Anything I leave out gets a default,
so this text sits centered in its box.

40
00:02:24,148 --> 00:02:25,818
The date line I'll paste.

41
00:02:25,882 --> 00:02:32,602
Same shape, at y 92, under the
title: {{date}}, 14 point, in gray.

42
00:02:32,809 --> 00:02:34,879
Title comes with every page.

43
00:02:34,910 --> 00:02:39,000
Date doesn't: it's a field I made
up, so Monday has to supply it.

44
00:02:39,112 --> 00:02:42,201
In its data: date, October 26.

45
00:02:42,752 --> 00:02:49,210
Then the lined paper, pasted: one
rectangle, 515 by 660 points.

46
00:02:49,254 --> 00:02:54,466
Fill type pattern, with lines h,
horizontal lines, every 24 points.

47
00:02:54,543 --> 00:02:56,493
Fill is the color of the lines.

48
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:59,870
Preview again, and open
the card to see it larger.

49
00:02:59,968 --> 00:03:03,518
Monday, October 26, and lines to write on.

50
00:03:03,727 --> 00:03:05,717
One page proves the template.

51
00:03:05,814 --> 00:03:09,724
Now the real shape: a week
page, with seven days under it.

52
00:03:09,934 --> 00:03:15,114
The week needs a template of its own,
pasted above the day so it's listed first:

53
00:03:15,114 --> 00:03:17,824
id week, name Week, and a wider title.

54
00:03:17,872 --> 00:03:19,512
Its list comes later.

55
00:03:19,716 --> 00:03:21,506
Preview shows something new.

56
00:03:21,586 --> 00:03:26,816
The Week card says Unused: the template
exists, but no page asks for it yet.

57
00:03:26,953 --> 00:03:28,763
It's a hint, not an error.

58
00:03:29,544 --> 00:03:32,274
So the root becomes the week: type week.

59
00:03:32,414 --> 00:03:35,744
Its title, Meals this week,
and no date of its own.

60
00:03:37,327 --> 00:03:41,887
Next, the day names, pasted: a
list of seven, counted from zero.

61
00:03:42,001 --> 00:03:45,481
Days of zero is Monday,
and days of six is Sunday.

62
00:03:45,687 --> 00:03:47,267
And the loop, pasted.

63
00:03:47,412 --> 00:03:52,762
for (let i = 0; i < 7; i++): the lines
inside run seven times, once per day.

64
00:03:52,967 --> 00:03:58,227
New Date, with year 2026,
month nine, and day 26 plus i.

65
00:03:58,352 --> 00:04:01,462
Months count from zero,
so nine is October.

66
00:04:01,666 --> 00:04:04,716
When i is six, that's October the 32nd.

67
00:04:04,838 --> 00:04:09,504
Date rolls it over to November the 1st,
so the end of the month takes care of

68
00:04:09,504 --> 00:04:10,178
itself.

69
00:04:10,382 --> 00:04:13,906
dateText turns that into
words: toLocaleDateString,

70
00:04:13,906 --> 00:04:18,232
in US English, with the long
month name and the day number.

71
00:04:18,289 --> 00:04:19,909
October 26.

72
00:04:20,113 --> 00:04:24,113
createId, with the prefix day,
makes a new id every time:

73
00:04:24,113 --> 00:04:27,872
day, an underscore, and
random letters and digits.

74
00:04:27,994 --> 00:04:29,924
It only exists in this script.

75
00:04:30,128 --> 00:04:33,728
Then the page itself:
parentId root, and type day.

76
00:04:33,787 --> 00:04:37,717
Its title is days of i, and
the dateText goes in its data.

77
00:04:37,804 --> 00:04:41,004
id on its own is short for id: id.

78
00:04:41,209 --> 00:04:44,059
Push adds the new id to
the root's children.

79
00:04:44,099 --> 00:04:48,929
That list is the page order, and it has
to agree with each page's parentId.

80
00:04:49,134 --> 00:04:51,624
Preview: two templates and eight pages.

81
00:04:51,770 --> 00:04:56,060
Meals this week uses the Week
template, and seven pages use Day.

82
00:04:57,306 --> 00:05:01,626
The week page needs its list: a
grid, pasted under its title.

83
00:05:01,712 --> 00:05:07,541
For a grid, w and h are the
size of one cell, 515 by 56.

84
00:05:07,746 --> 00:05:11,426
cols: 1: one cell per row, 8 points apart.

85
00:05:11,495 --> 00:05:16,065
Source type current: the cells come from
the children of the page being drawn.

86
00:05:16,133 --> 00:05:18,849
On Meals this week, that's the seven days.

87
00:05:19,054 --> 00:05:27,347
Display field is the pattern for
each cell: {{title}} · {{date}}.

88
00:05:27,408 --> 00:05:31,157
Each cell fills it in from its
own day, and links to that page.

89
00:05:31,361 --> 00:05:32,711
Now the way back.

90
00:05:32,759 --> 00:05:37,239
On the day page, after the date, a
small text, an arrow and Week, pasted.

91
00:05:37,364 --> 00:05:39,274
Its link target is parent.

92
00:05:39,482 --> 00:05:42,222
Parent means the page this one sits under.

93
00:05:42,366 --> 00:05:44,386
For every day, that's the week.

94
00:05:44,432 --> 00:05:49,396
No page numbers anywhere: the export
works them out when it writes the PDF.

95
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:50,600
Preview.

96
00:05:50,698 --> 00:05:53,418
The week lists all seven
days with their dates.

97
00:05:53,519 --> 00:05:56,349
And each day has its way
back, at the top right.

98
00:05:59,678 --> 00:06:02,668
Before I make this real,
a mistake on purpose.

99
00:06:02,717 --> 00:06:05,417
In the loop, I'll misspell day as 'dya'.

100
00:06:06,725 --> 00:06:08,675
This time no preview opens.

101
00:06:08,754 --> 00:06:12,241
The red text says hierarchy:
a node, by its id,

102
00:06:12,241 --> 00:06:15,384
references unknown template type 'dya'.

103
00:06:15,584 --> 00:06:18,984
It names the page that failed,
and the name it couldn't find.

104
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:22,069
A misspelled template name
stops the run like this.

105
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:24,240
It never shows up as Unused.

106
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:28,190
Three letters fix it, and the
red text goes as soon as I type.

107
00:06:28,422 --> 00:06:31,192
The other mistake you'll
make is a missing comma.

108
00:06:31,244 --> 00:06:35,114
I'll take out the one after
font size 14, in the date line.

109
00:06:38,287 --> 00:06:42,947
Template script, line 13:
Unexpected identifier 'textColor'.

110
00:06:43,005 --> 00:06:45,005
It names the script and the line.

111
00:06:45,206 --> 00:06:50,976
On line 13, the trouble sits just before
the word it names: the comma I took out.

112
00:06:51,011 --> 00:06:52,781
Comma back, and it's gone.

113
00:06:53,421 --> 00:06:54,781
Preview once more.

114
00:06:54,837 --> 00:06:57,047
There are two ways to use the result.

115
00:06:57,078 --> 00:07:00,497
Replace Current Project
swaps it into this project,

116
00:07:00,497 --> 00:07:03,898
after a confirmation, as
one step you can undo.

117
00:07:04,104 --> 00:07:09,133
Create As New Project leaves Kitchen
notes alone and opens a new project.

118
00:07:09,278 --> 00:07:10,898
I'll call it Meal planner.

119
00:07:11,103 --> 00:07:15,813
Here it is, in its own tab: eight
pages from 34 lines of code.

120
00:07:15,936 --> 00:07:19,446
Wednesday has its date, in the
data field the loop wrote.

121
00:07:19,648 --> 00:07:21,938
The scripts are saved with this project.

122
00:07:21,980 --> 00:07:26,703
Open the generator here, and the Preset
menu reads Current saved source,

123
00:07:26,703 --> 00:07:28,790
with a Saved Generator mark.

124
00:07:28,995 --> 00:07:31,395
The note above the editors says the rest.

125
00:07:31,487 --> 00:07:34,767
Publish the project, and the
scripts go public with it.

126
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:38,162
Opening them never runs
them; only Preview does.

127
00:07:38,375 --> 00:07:41,375
And hand edits on the canvas
aren't written back here.

128
00:07:41,419 --> 00:07:46,234
Run Replace again later, and it rebuilds
from these scripts, over those edits.

129
00:07:47,462 --> 00:07:50,272
Export PDF, and every link works.

130
00:07:50,326 --> 00:07:54,576
Friday's row goes to Friday, and
the arrow comes back to the week.

131
00:07:55,455 --> 00:07:58,235
You don't have to write
every line yourself, either.

132
00:07:58,270 --> 00:08:03,373
At the bottom of the generator, LLM Helper
& Schema Documentation holds a prompt

133
00:08:03,373 --> 00:08:04,963
written for chatbots.

134
00:08:05,178 --> 00:08:08,867
It teaches a chatbot everything
we did today: both scripts,

135
00:08:08,867 --> 00:08:13,618
every kind of element, link targets,
and what each script has to return.

136
00:08:13,721 --> 00:08:15,971
Copy puts all of it on your clipboard.

137
00:08:18,363 --> 00:08:21,860
Schema Reference, the other
tab, is the short version:

138
00:08:21,860 --> 00:08:25,866
every property of a template
and of a page, in two tables.

139
00:08:31,255 --> 00:08:36,375
Paste it into the chatbot you use, and
replace the placeholder on its last line with

140
00:08:36,375 --> 00:08:37,478
what you want.

141
00:08:37,607 --> 00:08:42,850
Mine asks for a habit tracker for November:
a month page that links to every day,

142
00:08:42,850 --> 00:08:46,207
and a page for each day
with ten habits to tick.

143
00:08:46,411 --> 00:08:48,211
The answer is two scripts.

144
00:08:48,251 --> 00:08:52,721
The first goes in Define Templates,
the second in Build Hierarchy.

145
00:08:52,788 --> 00:08:58,255
Then Preview, as always: nothing runs
before that, and the project isn't touched.

146
00:08:58,461 --> 00:09:01,877
Two templates, a month
calendar and a day page,

147
00:09:01,877 --> 00:09:04,962
and 31 pages: November and its 30 days.

148
00:09:05,107 --> 00:09:10,248
If Preview goes red instead, paste the
message back to the chatbot and ask for a

149
00:09:10,248 --> 00:09:10,755
fix.

150
00:09:10,826 --> 00:09:13,046
And read what it wrote before you use it.

151
00:09:13,114 --> 00:09:15,788
After today, you know
what every line does.

152
00:09:15,992 --> 00:09:19,412
Another week is one changed
date and a Preview away.

153
00:09:19,478 --> 00:09:24,018
Next time, we leave the editor: the
gallery, accounts, and saving to the cloud.
